.TH "GH-RELEASE.SH" "1" "November 2026" "arran4/dotfiles" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gh\-release.sh \- calculate and push a version tag for GitHub Actions publishing
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBgh\-release.sh [GIT\-TAG\-INC\-ARGS...]\fR
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Use git\-tag\-inc to calculate the next version and create its tag, then push the tag to origin. If the current commit has already been released, recognise the unchanged\-commit diagnostic and skip tagging. GitHub Actions, not this script, creates the GitHub release and its assets.
.SH NOTES
The helper retries a failed git push once. If both attempts fail it removes the locally created tag.
.PP
Release modes, force rebuilds, and publish\-tag recovery are handled by .github/workflows/ci.yml; this script is only the tagging path.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
Requires a Git checkout, git-tag-inc on PATH, push access to origin
and appropriate release-tag permissions. Inspect existing tags and
the checked-out commit before running. GitHub Actions needs its own
workflow permissions to publish the resulting release; see
dotfiles-ci(7).
.SH RELEASE SEQUENCE
The helper obtains the next tag via git-tag-inc -print-version-only,
creates the tag and pushes it. If the commit is unchanged since the
previous release, it recognises the diagnostic and exits without a
new tag. It retries a failed push once, then deletes the local tag
if the retry fails. It does not delete any remote tag.
.PP
The GitHub Actions workflow, not gh-release.sh, creates release assets,
release notes and container images. Manual release modes in ci.yml are
alternatives to this local tagging helper.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
git status --short
git tag --list 'v*'
gh-release.sh
gh workflow run ci.yml --repo arran4/dotfiles --ref main \
  -f mode=release-patch
.fi
.SH TROUBLESHOOTING
Use git-tag-inc -dry to investigate version selection. Check origin
access and tag protection rules for failed pushes. Do not overwrite
a published release tag to rebuild an image; use the publish-tag
recovery mode described in dotfiles-ci(7).
.SH SEE ALSO
git\-tag\-inc(1), git(1)
